  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-12T01:59:29.578Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the current control bindings, it's easy to forget that you have the action menu open and hit random gestures when trying to move. One way this could be addressed would be to set up the control bindings so that we could e.g. click the thumbstick to open the action menu, then keep it open as long as the thumbstick capacitative touch sensor is active (this would work for index, oculus, and vive at a minimum).\nUnfortunately with the current bindings it's not possible to do so; SteamVR input bindings don't support a \"release\" action for the touch sensor, and in any case there isn't a separate open and close action. Adding in additional bindings which would allow this control scheme to be bound would be really useful.",
